  "notes": [
   "Parts are unchanged from step 1, except that the open-ended USB cable's conducts now list one group (usb-a, positive, negative) instead of through pairs, since a cable is a plain connector.",
   "The pump is wired as the tutorial says: open-ended cable positive to relay 1 NO, pump positive (pump port 1, the supply side) to relay 1 COM, and the cable negative joined to the pump negative (port 2). The relay switches the pump's positive supply.",
   "The carrier has a single A6 port for the Grove connector, so the Grove cable's four conductors are shown as one connection from grove1 A1 to carrier A6. The sensor end is wired pin by pin (B1 SIG, B2 NC, B3 VCC, B4 GND).",
   "The MKR WiFi 1010 sits on the carrier's MKR socket. The Carrier is powered through the MKR board's USB port from the micro-USB cable.",
   "The usb-power-adapter type has only one USB-A port (A), so both USB cables go to port A as a simplification. The tutorial says the adapter has at least 2 USB ports.",
   "Relay 1 is the one used in the circuit text, although the code drives opla.Relay2. The circuit text and image take priority, so relay 1 is wired.",
   "The wire-to-relay connections use screw terminals (tool), and the cable negative to pump negative is a twisted join or connector strip (hand)."
  ]
 },
